[size=4][b]Description[/b][/size]
[size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Companion & Romance Roadmap[/b] is a live, in-game checklist for every companion's personal quest and romance, read straight from your save.

Most of what matters for a companion is easy to miss: a conversation you never had, a long rest you skipped, an area you can never go back to. Wikis tell you what [i]can[/i] happen. This mod tells you, inside the game, what has already happened in your playthrough and what is still open.

Press [b]F7[/b] and pick a companion:[/color][/size]
[list]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Where you stand[/b]: recruited, dating, partnered or lost, with live approval and its tier.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]What to do next[/b]: every step of their quest and romance, act by act. Where to go, what to do, what to avoid, rewards, and the approval each step needs next to yours. The next step is highlighted.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]What you are about to lose[/b]: the [i]Before you move on[/i] tab lists every upcoming point of no return and what is still open before it, and when the game itself asks "are you sure?" before one, the same list pops up right then.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Tonight at camp[/b]: which camp scenes play if you rest now, and what the others are still waiting for ("needs 40 approval with Shadowheart, you have 31").[/color][/size][/*]
[/list][size=3][color=#D4D4D8]Steps tick themselves off as you play. Everything is read from the game's own journal, story flags and approval values, so nothing is guessed, and the mod never changes your game.

[b][color=#e0a45c]Work in progress:[/color][/b] this is an early release. The guide and its detection keep improving with every update, and you may run into bugs or steps that are not detected yet. Some moments only exist inside a conversation and leave no trace in the save. The roadmap remembers the ones it sees happen; anything that was over before you installed it shows as [i]Not seen[/i], and you can check it off by hand. Please report anything wrong on the Bugs tab or on [url=https://github.com/Lumpish-Haggard/CompanionRoadmap/issues/new/choose]GitHub[/url]. The report file helps most: in the roadmap window choose [b]Options > Create a report file[/b], then attach it on GitHub or paste its contents.

[b]New in 1.2:[/b] [i]Tonight at camp[/i] reads the game's own camp-scene scheduler and tells you which scenes play at your next long rest, what the others still need, and which are about to run out. When the game asks whether you are ready to pass a point of no return, a heads-up shows what is still open right then. You can mark a romance as [i]Not interested[/i] (thanks for the request!): its steps then only show where it can begin, as [i]Say no[/i], and its notices stop. Steps that need an item say whether you have it (Night Orchid, Spear of Night, Infernal Iron and more), each companion's page lists their recent approval changes, and a reminder pops up when a fight starts against Minthara or Minsc while you can still knock them out. 1.1 taught the roadmap to remember what it has seen, to say why a companion left and to follow each companion's mood in their portrait. 1.0.2 added every way to lose a companion as golden rules; what was reviewed is listed on [url=https://github.com/Lumpish-Haggard/CompanionRoadmap/blob/main/docs/COVERAGE.md]GitHub[/url] (spoilers).

Open source (MIT): [url=https://github.com/Lumpish-Haggard/CompanionRoadmap]github.com/Lumpish-Haggard/CompanionRoadmap[/url][/color][/size]

[size=4][b]Installation instructions[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8]Install the [url=https://github.com/Norbyte/bg3se/releases]BG3 Script Extender[/url] if you have not already.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8]Install this mod with your mod manager:[/color]
[/size]
[list]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]BG3 Mod Manager[/b]: import the zip, move [i]Companion & Romance Roadmap[/i] to the active list, then save and export the load order.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Vortex[/b]: install, enable, deploy.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Manual[/b]: put [i]CompanionRoadmap.pak[/i] in [i]%LOCALAPPDATA%\Larian Studios\Baldur's Gate 3\Mods[/i] and enable it in your mod manager.[/color][/size][/*]
[/list][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8]Load a save and press [b]F7[/b]. With Mod Configuration Menu installed you can also open it from the mod's MCM page.[/color][/size][/*]
[/list][size=3][color=#D4D4D8]It is safe to add in the middle of a playthrough: the roadmap reads what the game has already recorded.
To uninstall, disable or remove it. Saves made with it still load; the game only warns that a mod is missing.[/color][/size]

[size=4][b]Main features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8]All [b]10 recruitable companions[/b] and around [b]100 steps[/b]: Shadowheart, Minthara, Karlach, Lae'zel, Astarion, Gale, Wyll, Halsin, Jaheira and Minsc.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Golden rules[/b] on every page: the choices that make that companion die or leave for good, plus a short list that applies to all of them. They follow your spoiler setting.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Your choice of path[/b]: where a story splits (Minthara: knock her out, or raid the Grove with her), both paths are shown as equals, each with what it changes.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Live statuses[/b] (Next, To do, Optional, Not seen, Waiting, Later, Done, Checked, Missed, N/A), updated within half a second. Hover a status to see what it means.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Points of no return[/b]: entering the Shadowfell (Act 1 locks), the Mind Flayer Colony, leaving for Baldur's Gate, the Lower City and the final battle, each with what you would still lose. Click an entry to jump to that step. When the game asks "are you sure?" before one, a heads-up shows that list right then.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Tonight at camp[/b]: the roadmap reads the game's own camp-scene scheduler, so it knows which scenes play at your next long rest, what holds back the others (approval, being their partner, a story moment still to come, a more important scene first) and which are about to run out.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Not interested[/b] in a romance? Tick it on the companion's page. Their romance steps then only show where it can begin, so you know which conversation to turn it down in, and their romance notices stop.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Do you have the item?[/b] Steps that need one say whether your party has it, camp chest included: Night Orchid, Spear of Night, Infernal Iron, Orphic Hammer and more.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Recent approval changes[/b] on every companion's page: by how much, who you were talking to, and how many long rests ago.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Knock out, do not kill[/b]: a reminder when a fight starts against Minthara or Minsc while you can still recruit them.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Hidden trackers[/b]: Shadowheart's Nightsong points (4 of 6 make sparing Nightsong far easier), Karlach's engine upgrades and the magic items fed to Gale.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]The easy-to-miss details[/b]: Shadowheart's wolf memory (needed for the Act 3 swim), Minthara's non-lethal knockout rules, Karlach's Act 2 night, Gale's starry night before the Colony, Wyll's party-only romance start, Astarion's ascension checks, and more.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Notifications[/b] when a romance or important step is completed or missed, wherever you want them on screen.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Manual check-offs[/b] for moments the game does not record or another mod changes. They are saved in your savegame.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]It remembers[/b]: once the roadmap has seen a step happen, the step stays done even if the game clears its own record later, and it tells you that it is remembered.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Spoiler control[/b]: the roadmap asks once how much it may reveal about later acts (everything, step titles only, or nothing). Until you choose, later acts stay hidden.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Companion portraits that react[/b] (can be switched off): the game's own Photo Mode stickers, changing with approval, romance and whether the companion is alive.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]One-click report file[/b] for bug reports: it lists what the tracker sees in your save, game identifiers only.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Looks like it belongs in BG3[/b]: a quiet dark panel in the game's own Quadraat typeface, with colour only where it means something.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Mod Configuration Menu[/b] support: a settings page, a rebindable hotkey and an [i]Open roadmap[/i] button. Without MCM, every option is in the window's Options tab.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Multiplayer and origin aware[/b]: each player sees their own approval and romance, and playing as an origin marks that companion's recruitment and romance as not applicable.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Plays nicely with other mods[/b]: romance mods such as PolyamoryFixes and NoRomanceLimit work (check a step off by hand if a mod changes how it is recorded). Mods that rewrite a companion's story, such as Really Shadowheart, should still be detected, but the guide describes the unmodded game; details on GitHub. The mod is read-only: it never changes flags, approval, quests or items.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8]Default key [b]F7[/b]. F8 is deliberately avoided because it is the game's Quickload.[/color][/size][/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][url=https://github.com/Norbyte/bg3se/releases]BG3 Script Extender[/url]: [b]required[/b], v25 or newer.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/baldursgate3/mods/9162]Mod Configuration Menu[/url]: optional, for a settings page, a rebindable hotkey and an Open roadmap button.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8]Baldur's Gate 3 Patch 8. The guide data is verified against the Patch 8 Hotfix 10 game files.[/color][/size][/*]
[/list][size=3][color=#D4D4D8]The roadmap's text is in English only for now.[/color][/size]

